      "source": [
        "### **Analyzing Cancellations & Negative Quantities**\n",
        "In retail datasets, negative values in `Quantity` usually indicate cancelled transactions or returns. Often, cancelled invoice numbers start with the letter 'C'. verifying this and checking the proportion of cancellations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 162
        },
        "id": "edec2f3a",
        "outputId": "ef47d221-9854-41c6-afd6-8a265bf697c6"
      },
      "source": [
        "# invoices with negative quantities start with 'C'\n",
        "df['is_cancelled'] = df['Invoice'].str.startswith('C', na=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "cancel_summary = df.groupby('is_cancelled')['Quantity'].agg(['count', 'min', 'max', 'mean'])\n",
        "display(cancel_summary)\n",
        "\n",
        "# Proportion of cancellations\n",
        "cancel_pct = (df['is_cancelled'].sum() / len(df)) * 100\n",
        "print(f\"Percentage of cancelled/returned transactions: {cancel_pct:.2f}%\")"
      ],
      "execution_count": 33,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "display_data",
