      "source": [
        "### **2. Scanning for Test and Non-Product Stock Codes**\n",
        "Retail databases often contain non-product entries (like postage, manual adjustments, samples, or developer tests) embedded in the `StockCode` or `Description` columns. We will identify the most frequent non-numeric stock codes."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {
        "colab": {
          "base_uri": "https://localhost:8080/",
          "height": 413
        },
        "id": "d636dbe6",
        "outputId": "f888940b-a37b-408d-e950-d5c4a60575e3"
      },
      "source": [
        "# Get non-numeric stock codes (codes containing letters)\n",
        "non_numeric_stock = df[df['StockCode'].str.contains('[A-Za-z]', na=False, regex=True)]\n",
        "\n",
        "non_numeric_summary = (\n",
        "    non_numeric_stock.groupby('StockCode')['Description']\n",
        "    .unique()\n",
        "    .to_frame()\n",
        "    .join(non_numeric_stock['StockCode'].value_counts().to_frame(name='Occurrence_Count'))\n",
        "    .sort_values(by='Occurrence_Count', ascending=False)\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"--- NON-PRODUCT OR SPECIAL TRANSACTION CODES ---\")\n",
        "display(non_numeric_summary.head(10))"
      ],
