    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "ae610a20"
      },
      "source": [
        "## **Key Insights & Executive Summary of the EDA**\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on our comprehensive exploratory data analysis of the retail dataset, here are the main findings and anomalies discovered:\n",
        "\n",
        "### **1. Missing Customer Identifiers**\n",
        "* **Magnitude**: Approximately **19.87%** of transactions do not have a recorded `Customer ID`.\n",
        "* **Geographic Pattern**: These unidentified transactions are overwhelmingly concentrated in the **United Kingdom**, followed by **EIRE**.\n",
        "* **Associated Products**: Unidentified transactions are highly associated with service items like **'DOTCOM POSTAGE'** and **'Manual'** entries.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **2. Cancellations & Returns**\n",
        "* **Cancellations**: Cancelled orders (indicated by Invoice numbers starting with **'C'**) make up **1.97%** of all transactions.\n",
        "* **Impact**: Returned items show massive negative quantities (reaching as low as **-7,128** units), which skew average order sizes if not isolated.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **3. Irregular Prices & Non-Sales Transactions**\n",
        "* **Zero & Negative Prices**: There are **3,483** transactions with a price of zero or less. Their descriptions (e.g., `'damaged'`, `'missing'`, `'?'`, `'given away'`) indicate these are non-sales adjustment records, bad debt write-offs, or inventory corrections.\n",
        "* **Manual Overhead**: The highest unit prices in the dataset belong to **'Manual'** overrides and **'BANK CHARGES'**, reaching up to **£25,111.09**.\n",
        "\n",
        "### **4. Seasonal Trends & Top Sellers**\n",
        "* **Seasonality**: Monthly revenue remains relatively stable around **£550k - £850k** during the year, but experiences a massive surge in **October (£1.16M)** and **November (£1.09M)** due to peak holiday shopping.\n",
        "* **Top Revenue Drivers**: `'Manual'` booking charges, `'WHITE HANGING HEART T-LIGHT HOLDER'`, and `'REGENCY CAKESTAND 3 TIER'` are the top financial contributors to total revenue."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "fd1644e9"
      },
      "source": [
        "## **Top 5 Critical Questions Raised by This EDA**\n",
        "\n",
        "Based on our exploratory findings, here are the most important business and data processing questions we must address before proceeding to modeling or advanced analytics:\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **How should we treat transactions with missing Customer IDs?**  \n",
        "   Since unidentified customers make up nearly **20%** of our data, should we isolate them into a separate group, impute them, or discard them depending on whether our goal is user-level recommendation or overall inventory forecasting?\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **How do we handle 'Manual' overrides and bookkeeping entries?**  \n",
        "   Transactions flagged with `'M'` (Manual) and `'BANK CHARGES'` dominate our high-price outlier list and top-revenue lists. Are these actual sales, or should they be excluded from consumer purchasing behavior models?\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Should we filter out extreme bulk orders or treat them as a distinct customer segment?**  \n",
        "   We observed single transactions with quantities exceeding **10,000+** units. Do these represents B2B wholesale buyers that need to be modeled separately from typical retail consumers?\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **What is the best way to handle cancellations and returns?**  \n",
        "   Should we structurally pair and neutralize each cancelled transaction (invoices starting with `'C'`) with its original purchase record, or treat them as a continuous rate of return?\n",
        "\n",
        "5. **What is causing the major revenue surge in October and November?**  \n",
        "   Does this massive volume spike represent holiday seasonal shopping (Halloween/Christmas stock-up), and how should we adjust inventory levels to prevent stockouts during this high-demand period?"
      ]
    }
  ]

